			<div class="content" id="post-content-3582477">
									

<p>I realize now that it might be a bit unclear, but the sentence talking about the perimeter indicates that one is only established when the turtle surfaces, which is rare. Plus, I think you'd only need a perimeter of 3-4 boats to actively patrol the turtle, and they're mostly there to ward off GoIs as opposed to random civilians.</p>
<p>I also say in the article that the turtle is in hiding, because it's smart enough to know that if it compromises consensus reality, bad things will probably happen to it. If it were to surface in a populated area, then yeah, the Foundation would have to deploy amnestics (not sure why they'd have to sink civilians boats), but this is preparing for a scenario that has not ever happened, the Foundation has good reason to believe will not happen, and that has an obvious response, so I didn't include it in the containment procedures.</p>

